{# What the plates below it count, counted once.

   COVERAGE is the sum of the zones' geodesic areas over the AOI's own — and that shortcut is only
   sound because zones never share interior, so the union's area IS the sum of the parts. It can be
   under 100%: an area is often only partly zoned, and a gap is legal.

   The design's fourth plate is "Last import" (file, date, who). The host records none of that
   today — a Zone carries no provenance — so the plate that ships instead is the one the data can
   actually answer: how much of the area is not in any zone. Inventing an import date would be
   worse than not showing one.

   AN UNZONED AREA still counts honestly. The dashboard only draws this widget where zones exist
   (the surface is presence-driven), but the library renders every widget whatever the area holds:
   with none, the counts are real zeros — nothing IS zoned — and the one plate that names a zone
   says there is none rather than inventing one. #}
<div data-w="kpis">
    <div class="grid g4">
        <div class="c kpi">
            <span class="tab"><span class="idx">PL·43</span>Zones</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ zones|length }}<em>defined</em></b>
            <span class="sub">never overlapping · edges may be shared</span>
        </div>
        <div class="c kpi{{ coveragePct >= 99.5 ? ' hot' }}">
            <span class="tab"><span class="idx">PL·44</span>AOI covered</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ coveragePct|number_format(1) }}<em>%</em></b>
            <span class="sub">{{ zonedKm2|number_format(0) }} km² of {{ areaKm2|number_format(0) }} km²</span>
        </div>
        {% set largest = zones|sort((a, b) => b.areaKm2 <=> a.areaKm2)|first %}
        <div class="c kpi">
            <span class="tab"><span class="idx">PL·45</span>Largest</span>
            {% if largest %}
                <b class="disp">{{ largest.name }}<em></em></b>
                <span class="sub">{{ largest.areaKm2|number_format(0) }} km² · {{ largest.sharePct|number_format(1) }}% of AOI</span>
            {% else %}
                <b class="disp mono d">—<em></em></b>
                <span class="sub">no zone to be the largest of</span>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="c kpi">
            <span class="tab"><span class="idx">PL·46</span>Unzoned</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ (100 - coveragePct)|number_format(1) }}<em>%</em></b>
            <span class="sub">a gap is legal · zones need not cover the AOI</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
